1
00:00:02,400 --> 00:00:07,000
They looked across the water and
believed Rome would shelter them.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Weapons were surrendered for a promise
of land and peace.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:18,000
The barrier closed. Fields and granaries
stayed visible beyond the fence.

4
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:25,000
Food became leverage. Bowls stayed empty
while grain was guarded.

5
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:31,000
A bronze horse clasp changed hands for a
crust of bread.

6
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:39,000
A brother was taken. The family broke in
plain sight.

7
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:46,000
She fed what was left of the child. A
torn scarf stayed in his fist.

8
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:51,000
Lupicinus offered a banquet — warmth
performed as reconciliation.

9
00:00:53,400 --> 00:00:56,000
Below the hall, Roman blades were
readied in secret.

10
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:01,000
The invitation was an execution dressed
as hospitality.

11
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:07,000
Fritigern took Lupicinus hostage before
the trap could close.

12
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:14,000
The hall became violence.

13
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:18,000
While spectacle held the room, the
counteroperation moved elsewhere.

14
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:24,000
Confiscated arms crossed the postern
gate in wagons.

15
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:30,000
Cloaked riders carried the weapons into
indigo night.

16
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:35,000
Fritigern left with Lupicinus still
alive.

17
00:01:37,400 --> 00:01:40,000
The stolen weapons reached a wooded
clearing.

18
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:46,000
Children, wounded, and elders waited
among the wagons.

19
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:54,000
Travel cloaks fell. Men trained to fight
stood in their place.

20
00:01:54,000 --> 00:02:00,000
Roman infantry approached as if
slaughtering refugees would be simple.

21
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:05,000
A young soldier saw what was forming
ahead — and understood too late.

22
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:11,000
Arrows found Roman shields.

23
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:17,000
Gothic shields drove the line backward.

24
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:22,000
Orders dissolved into noise.

25
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:27,000
An older Roman saw children beneath the
canvas.

26
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:33,000
Alaric watched without understanding
everything — only that it was terror.

27
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:40,000
The Roman formation fractured. The
Gothic line held.

28
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:47,000
Fritigern and Lupicinus fought toward
the wagons where families hid.

29
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:57,000
He had taken up the knife for his child.
He would not teach the child to worship

30
00:02:57,000 --> 00:03:03,000
Sunlight and flowers continued after the
violence fell away.

31
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:11,000
A damaged Roman helmet passed into the
child's hands — inheritance, not trophy.

32
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:16,000
